<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>The ultimate Silk Road overland adventure. From the turquoise domes of Samarkand to the 7,000m peaks of the Karakoram, this 23-day journey traces the footsteps of Marco Polo, Alexander the Great, and generations of Silk Road traders. Cross three countries — Uzbekistan, China, and Pakistan — on the world's highest paved international road. This is not just a tour; it's an expedition.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Registan Square at sunset in Samarkand</li><li>Bukhara's 1,000-year-old trading domes</li>
      <li>Khiva — a living museum inside ancient walls</li>
      <li>Kashgar's legendary Sunday Bazaar</li>
      <li>Drive the Karakoram Highway past 7,000m peaks</li>
      <li>Hunza Valley — Shangri-La of the Karakoram</li>
      <li>Baltit & Altit Forts (700+ years old)</li>
      <li>Rakaposhi (7,788m) and Nanga Parbat (8,126m)</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Tashkent, Uzbekistan</h4><p>Welcome to Uzbekistan. Airport transfer, hotel check-in. Evening walk through Amir Timur Square and Independence Square. Welcome dinner with plov (Uzbekistan's national dish).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Tashkent 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent — Modern Capital, Ancient Roots</h4><p>Visit Khast Imam Complex housing the world's oldest Quran. Explore Chorsu Bazaar — a sensory overload of spices, breads, and silk. Afternoon at the Museum of Applied Arts.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Tashkent 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent &#128646; Samarkand (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning Afrosiyob train to Samarkand (2 hrs). Afternoon: first view of Registan Square — three madrasahs with turquoise domes that have inspired travelers for 600 years.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Samarkand 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand — The Heart of the Silk Road</h4><p>Full day in Timur's capital. Visit Gur-e-Amir Mausoleum, Bibi-Khanym Mosque, and Shah-i-Zinda necropolis — the "Street of Tombs." Examine silk paper-making at Konigil village.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Samarkand 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand &#8594; Bukhara</h4><p>Drive through the Kyzylkum Desert to Bukhara (4 hrs). Afternoon stroll through Lyabi-Hauz — a 400-year-old plaza centered on a reflecting pool, surrounded by madrasahs and茶馆s.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bukhara 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara — 1,000 Years of Trade</h4><p>Visit the Ark Fortress, Kalon Minaret (Genghis Khan spared it), and the three remaining trading domes. Afternoon at Chor Minor and a carpet-weaving workshop.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bukhara 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara &#8594; Khiva (Across the Kyzylkum)</h4><p>Long but spectacular drive across the Kyzylkum Desert (7 hrs) to Khiva. Arrive at sunset when the mud-brick walls glow golden. Dinner on a rooftop overlooking the minarets.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Khiva 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva — Living Museum</h4><p>Full day inside Itchan Kala — the inner walled city. Climb the Islam Khoja Minaret for panoramic views. Visit the unfinished Kalta Minor Minaret with its stunning turquoise tiles.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Khiva 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva &#8594; Urgench &#9992; Tashkent &#9992; Kashgar</h4><p>Morning transfer to Urgench Airport. Flights via Tashkent to Kashgar, China. Border formalities at Kashgar Airport. Rest after the journey.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Bazaar & Old City</h4><p>If it's Sunday: the legendary bazaar. If not: explore Kashgar Old City — mud-brick houses, craft workshops, and 100-year-old teahouses. Evening Uyghur music performance.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway Begins!</h4><p>Visit Id Kah Mosque and Abakh Khoja Tomb in the morning. Afternoon drive to Karakul Lake (3,600m) on the legendary Karakoram Highway. Camp or lodge at the lake with views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Karakul Lodge</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Karakul Lake &#8594; Tashkurgan</h4><p>Dawn photography at the lake, then continue south. Visit the Tajik-style Stone Fort in Tashkurgan (3,100m). Explore grasslands where Marco Polo's sheep still graze.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Tashkurgan 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Cross the Khunjerab Pass! China &#8594; Pakistan</h4><p>The big day. Drive to Khunjerab Pass (4,693m) — the highest paved border crossing in the world. Clear Chinese exit and Pakistani entry formalities. Descend into Pakistan's Hunza Valley — the fabled Shangri-La.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Karimabad 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Hunza Valley — Baltit & Altit Forts</h4><p>Explore the 700-year-old Baltit Fort with panoramic views of the Hunza Valley. Visit Altit Fort, even older. Afternoon: apricot orchard walk and local Hunza cuisine.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Karimabad 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Hunza — Rakaposhi Base Camp Trek</h4><p>Day trek to Rakaposhi Base Camp (moderate, 4-5 hrs). Stand in awe before Rakaposhi's 7,788m north face — one of the most dramatic mountain walls on Earth. Return to Karimabad.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Karimabad 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Karimabad &#8594; Passu Cones &#8594; Gulmit</h4><p>Drive to the iconic Passu Cones — jagged cathedral-like peaks that define the Karakoram skyline. Visit Borith Lake and the Hussaini suspension bridge (one of the world's most dangerous!).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Gulmit Lodge</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>17</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Gulmit &#8594; Gilgit</h4><p>Drive along the Hunza River to Gilgit (3 hrs). Visit the 7th-century Kargah Buddha carving. Afternoon at Gilgit Bazaar — the commercial hub of Pakistan's northern territories.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Gilgit 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>18</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Gilgit &#8594; Fairy Meadows (Nanga Parbat)</h4><p>Drive to Raikot Bridge, then take a heart-stopping jeep ride to Tato Village. 3-hour trek to Fairy Meadows — one of the most beautiful alpine meadows on Earth, facing the mighty Nanga Parbat (8,126m).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Fairy Meadows Hut</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>19</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Fairy Meadows — Nanga Parbat Base Camp</h4><p>Dawn view of Nanga Parbat — the "Killer Mountain." Optional trek to Nanga Parbat Base Camp (6 hrs return). Or simply relax and soak in the majesty of the world's 9th highest peak.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Fairy Meadows Hut</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>20</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Fairy Meadows &#8594; Besham</h4><p>Trek down, jeep to Raikot Bridge, then drive the Karakoram Highway south along the Indus River. Overnight in Besham, the halfway point on the ancient trade route to the plains.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Besham 2&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>21</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Besham &#8594; Taxila &#8594; Islamabad</h4><p>Drive to Taxila — a UNESCO World Heritage site that was a major Buddhist learning center on the Silk Road. Explore the ruins, then continue to Islamabad.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Islamabad 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>22</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Islamabad — Faisal Mosque & Saidpur Village</h4><p>Visit Faisal Mosque, Pakistan's largest. Explore Lok Virsa Museum for Pakistani culture. Afternoon at Saidpur Village — a 500-year-old settlement turned cultural hub. Farewell dinner.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Islamabad 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>23</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Islamabad</h4><p>Airport transfer. Your epic Silk Road overland journey concludes. From the Registan to the Karakoram — you've traced the footsteps of history. &#1582;&#1583;&#1575;&#1581;&#1575;&#1601;&#1592;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

